<title>ITALY: Doubts on Italy EMU sustainability baseless - Micheli.</title>
<headline>Doubts on Italy EMU sustainability baseless - Micheli.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Doubts raised by Germany's Ifo research body that Italy lacks the sustainability needed for European economic and monetary union (EMU) are groundless, Cabinet undersecretary Enrico Micheli said.</p>
<p>&quot;Italy is doing very well, all the indicators are good and there are no reasons to have doubts,&quot; Micheli told reporters.</p>
<p>Ifo said on Monday that Italy may hit the 3.0 percent deficit/GDP EMU target but should nevertheless be kept out of the first round of euro nations until it proved its reliability on continued fiscal restraint.</p>
<p>Ifo noted Italian government plans to cut the budget deficit to 1.8 percent and debt to 116 percent of GDP by the year 2000, but it said this commitment should be proved before Italy joins the single currency.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
